"""JavaScript configuration.

The directory pages ship one script, and it is the only part of this repo a
browser executes rather than a toolchain we control. Nothing else here can
catch a mistake in it: a Go test renders the templates but never runs the
script, so a reference error or a sort that compares strings where it meant
numbers passes every other test and breaks only in a reader's browser.

No npm dependencies, and none intended — the script has none, so there is no
lockfile to keep pinned. This is the node toolchain, and esbuild to minify what
the browser is sent: the sources carry their reasoning in comments, and a
reader's browser has no use for any of it.
"""

bazel_dep(name = "aspect_rules_js", version = "3.4.1")
bazel_dep(name = "aspect_rules_esbuild", version = "0.27.0")

esbuild = use_extension("@aspect_rules_esbuild//esbuild:extensions.bzl", "esbuild")
esbuild.toolchain(esbuild_version = "0.28.0")
use_repo(esbuild, "esbuild_toolchains")
register_toolchains("@esbuild_toolchains//:all")
